 da
DESCRIPTION:Where: Instagram @kestreleye26\, shared to Facebook\, location
  tag: Canada\nType: Reel. Show in profile grid: OFF\nFile: design/social-
 and-merch/instagram-guides/12-days-reel.mp4 · cover design/social-and-me
 rch/instagram-guides/12-days-reel-cover.jpg (Edit cover\, Add from camera
  roll)\n- Music: add The Twelve Days of Christmas (feat. The Puppini Sist
 ers\; Bing Crosby\, The Andrews Sisters) in Instagram and keep the start 
 where Instagram puts it (the countdown from ten). The Reel is timed to it
 \; play it through once before sharing.\n- Facebook: before sharing\, tur
 n on Share to Facebook so it also goes to the kestreleye26 Page. Nothing 
 else to post there.\n\nCAPTION (copy and paste):\nOn the 12th day of Chri
 stmas… well\, here are 10 reasons to sign up to Kestrel.\n\nJobs only i
 n eye care. Every job says if it's an existing vacancy and if AI screens 
 candidates. No "Canadian experience" requirements. Clinic profiles to loo
 k around. Every job shows its pay. You apply for the roles that fit you\,
  get alerts for jobs that fit\, and track every application in 1 place.\n
 \nAnd a job board made for eye care in Canada. Pre launch is open: link i
 n bio.\n\n#12DaysOfChristmas #EyeCareJobs #Optometry #Opticians #CanadaJo
 bs\n\nALT TEXT (Advanced settings\, Accessibility):\nA short animation on
  a snowy navy night. A stylized kestrel in a holiday hat sits on top of a
  Christmas tree like the star. Numbers count down from 10 to 1\, each wit
 h a reason to join Kestrel\, as ornaments are added: baubles\, a gift\, a
  pair of glasses\, a trial lens\, gold rings\, an ophthalmoscope\, a cont
 act lens case and an eye chart tag. At 5\, in gold: Every job shows its p
 ay. At 1: and a job board made for eye care in Canada\, as the kestrel fl
 ies off the tree. Ends with the Kestrel Eye Care Jobs logo\, Pre launch i
 s open for candidates\, clinics and suppliers\, and Link in bio.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Post now: Instagram + Facebook\, Reel: The 12 days of Christma
 s (10 reasons)
