BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kestrel-social-20261228-reel-licence-fees-hours-of-work-by-province-v2
 @eyecarejobs.ca
DTSTAMP:20261128T153910Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T193000
SUMMARY:Instagram + Facebook: Reel: Licence fees: hours of work\, by provi
 nce
LOCATION:Instagram @kestreleye26\, shared to Facebook\, location tag: Cana
 da
DESCRIPTION:Where: Instagram @kestreleye26\, shared to Facebook\, location
  tag: Canada\nType: Reel. Show in profile grid: OFF\nFile: design/social-
 and-merch/instagram-guides/licence-reel.mp4 · cover design/social-and-me
 rch/instagram-guides/licence-reel-cover.jpg (Edit cover\, Add from camera
  roll)\n- Music: add Cornfield Chase (Hans Zimmer) in Instagram and drag 
 the start to 0:38 (Ontario starts filling as the orchestra swells). The R
 eel is timed to it\; play it through once before sharing.\n- Check the fe
 es in the optician pay guide are still current before posting.\n- If Onta
 rio opticians push back in the comments\, thank them and point to the gui
 de\; don't take sides on the fee.\n- Facebook: before sharing\, turn on S
 hare to Facebook so it also goes to the kestreleye26 Page. Nothing else t
 o post there.\n\nCAPTION (copy and paste):\nHow many hours does an optici
 an work just to pay for their licence?\n\nUsing each province's typical o
 ptician pay\, the yearly licence fee works out to about 18 to 19 hours of
  work in Nova Scotia\, and about 43 hours in Ontario\, where the fee is $
 1\,237.35 for 2027. That's more than twice Nova Scotia's fee\, for $1 an 
 hour less in typical pay.\n\nLicence fees fund the regulator's work prote
 cting patients. This is about seeing the full picture when you compare pa
 y between provinces.\n\nPay is only half the picture. Every province's pa
 y and licence fee is in our optician pay guide: link in bio.\n\nFees from
  each regulator's website\, November 2026. 5 provinces checked so far\, m
 ore coming.\n\n#Opticians #OpticianLife #EyeCareJobs #Ontario #CanadaJobs
 \n\nALT TEXT (Advanced settings\, Accessibility):\nA short animation on c
 ream. Text reads: How many hours does an optician work just to pay for th
 eir licence? Rows of small squares fill in\, 1 square for each hour of wo
 rk at the province's typical optician pay: Nova Scotia about 18 to 19 hou
 rs\, Alberta about 24 to 30\, Manitoba about 29 to 31\, British Columbia 
 about 35\, and Ontario about 43\, shown in chestnut. Text reads: Ontario'
 s fee is more than twice Nova Scotia's. Pay is only half the picture. End
 s with the Kestrel Eye Care Jobs logo and Link in bio.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Post now: Instagram + Facebook\, Reel: Licence fees: hours of 
 work\, by province
TRIGGER:PT0M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
